@node puppeteerdevices
@subsection puppeteer.devices
@findex puppeteer.devices
@anchor{#puppeteerdevices}
@itemize
@item
returns:
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object,Object}>
@end itemize

Returns a list of devices to be used with
@ref{#pageemulateoptions,@code{page.emulate(options)}}. Actual list of
devices can be found in
@uref{https://github.com/GoogleChrome/puppeteer/blob/master/lib/DeviceDescriptors.js,lib/DeviceDescriptors.js}.

@verbatim
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');
const iPhone = puppeteer.devices['iPhone 6'];

puppeteer.launch().then(async browser => {
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.emulate(iPhone);
  await page.goto('https://www.google.com');
  // other actions...
  await browser.close();
});
@end verbatim

@quotation
@strong{NOTE} The old way (Puppeteer versions <= v1.14.0) devices can be
obtained with @code{require('puppeteer/DeviceDescriptors')}.
@end quotation

@node puppeteererrors
@subsection puppeteer.errors
@findex puppeteer.errors
@anchor{#puppeteererrors}
@itemize
@item
returns:
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object,Object}>
@itemize
@item
@code{TimeoutError}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Function,function}>
A class of @ref{#class-timeouterror,TimeoutError}.
@end itemize

@end itemize

Puppeteer methods might throw errors if they are unable to fufill a
request. For example,
@ref{#pagewaitforselectorselector-options,page.waitForSelector(selector[,
options])} might fail if the selector doesn't match any nodes during the
given timeframe.

For certain types of errors Puppeteer uses specific error classes. These
classes are available via @ref{#puppeteererrors,@code{puppeteer.errors}}

An example of handling a timeout error:

@verbatim
try {
  await page.waitForSelector('.foo');
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof puppeteer.errors.TimeoutError) {
    // Do something if this is a timeout.
  }
}
@end verbatim

@quotation
@strong{NOTE} The old way (Puppeteer versions <= v1.14.0) errors can be
obtained with @code{require('puppeteer/Errors')}.
@end quotation

