@node class Page
@section class: Page
@anchor{#class-page}
@itemize
@item
extends:
@uref{https://nodejs.org/api/events.html#events_class_eventemitter,EventEmitter}
@end itemize

Page provides methods to interact with a single tab or
@uref{https://developer.chrome.com/extensions/background_pages,extension
background page} in Chromium. One @ref{#class-browser,Browser} instance
might have multiple @ref{#class-page,Page} instances.

This example creates a page, navigates it to a URL, and then saves a
screenshot:

@verbatim
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');

puppeteer.launch().then(async browser => {
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.goto('https://example.com');
  await page.screenshot({path: 'screenshot.png'});
  await browser.close();
});
@end verbatim

The Page class emits various events (described below) which can be
handled using any of Node's native
@uref{https://nodejs.org/api/events.html#events_class_eventemitter,@code{EventEmitter}}
methods, such as @code{on}, @code{once} or @code{removeListener}.

This example logs a message for a single page @code{load} event:

@verbatim
page.once('load', () => console.log('Page loaded!'));
@end verbatim

To unsubscribe from events use the @code{removeListener} method:

@verbatim
function logRequest(interceptedRequest) {
  console.log('A request was made:', interceptedRequest.url());
}
page.on('request', logRequest);
// Sometime later...
page.removeListener('request', logRequest);
@end verbatim

