@node pagepdf[options]
@subsection page.pdf([options])
@findex page.pdf
@anchor{#pagepdfoptions}
@itemize
@item
@code{options}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object,Object}>
Options object which might have the following properties:
@itemize
@item
@code{path}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}>
The file path to save the PDF to. If @code{path} is a relative path,
then it is resolved relative to
@uref{https://nodejs.org/api/process.html#process_process_cwd,current
working directory}. If no path is provided, the PDF won't be saved to
the disk.
@item
@code{scale}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type,number}>
Scale of the webpage rendering. Defaults to @code{1}. Scale amount must
be between 0.1 and 2.
@item
@code{displayHeaderFooter}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Boolean_type,boolean}>
Display header and footer. Defaults to @code{false}.
@item
@code{headerTemplate}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}>
HTML template for the print header. Should be valid HTML markup with
following classes used to inject printing values into them:
@itemize
@item
@code{date} formatted print date
@item
@code{title} document title
@item
@code{url} document location
@item
@code{pageNumber} current page number
@item
@code{totalPages} total pages in the document
@end itemize

@item
@code{footerTemplate}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}>
HTML template for the print footer. Should use the same format as the
@code{headerTemplate}.
@item
@code{printBackground}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Boolean_type,boolean}>
Print background graphics. Defaults to @code{false}.
@item
@code{landscape}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Boolean_type,boolean}>
Paper orientation. Defaults to @code{false}.
@item
@code{pageRanges}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}>
Paper ranges to print, e.g., `1-5, 8, 11-13'. Defaults to the empty
string, which means print all pages.
@item
@code{format}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}>
Paper format. If set, takes priority over @code{width} or @code{height}
options. Defaults to `Letter'.
@item
@code{width}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}|@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type,number}>
Paper width, accepts values labeled with units.
@item
@code{height}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}|@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type,number}>
Paper height, accepts values labeled with units.
@item
@code{margin}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object,Object}>
Paper margins, defaults to none.
@itemize
@item
@code{top}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}|@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type,number}>
Top margin, accepts values labeled with units.
@item
@code{right}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}|@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type,number}>
Right margin, accepts values labeled with units.
@item
@code{bottom}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}|@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type,number}>
Bottom margin, accepts values labeled with units.
@item
@code{left}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}|@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type,number}>
Left margin, accepts values labeled with units.
@end itemize

@item
@code{preferCSSPageSize}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Boolean_type,boolean}>
Give any CSS @code{@@page} size declared in the page priority over what
is declared in @code{width} and @code{height} or @code{format} options.
Defaults to @code{false}, which will scale the content to fit the paper
size.
@end itemize

@item
returns:
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise,Promise}<@uref{https://nodejs.org/api/buffer.html#buffer_class_buffer,Buffer}>>
Promise which resolves with PDF buffer.
@end itemize

@quotation
@strong{NOTE} Generating a pdf is currently only supported in Chrome
headless.
@end quotation
@code{page.pdf()} generates a pdf of the page with @code{print} css
media. To generate a pdf with @code{screen} media, call
@ref{#pageemulatemediamediatype,page.emulateMedia(`screen')} before
calling @code{page.pdf()}:

@quotation
@strong{NOTE} By default, @code{page.pdf()} generates a pdf with
modified colors for printing. Use the
@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/-webkit-print-color-adjust,@code{-webkit-print-color-adjust}}
property to force rendering of exact colors.
@end quotation

@verbatim
// Generates a PDF with 'screen' media type.
await page.emulateMedia('screen');
await page.pdf({path: 'page.pdf'});
@end verbatim

The @code{width}, @code{height}, and @code{margin} options accept values
labeled with units. Unlabeled values are treated as pixels.

A few examples: - @code{page.pdf(@{width: 100@})} - prints with width
set to 100 pixels - @code{page.pdf(@{width: '100px'@})} - prints with
width set to 100 pixels - @code{page.pdf(@{width: '10cm'@})} - prints
with width set to 10 centimeters.

All possible units are: - @code{px} - pixel - @code{in} - inch -
@code{cm} - centimeter - @code{mm} - millimeter

The @code{format} options are: - @code{Letter}: 8.5in x 11in -
@code{Legal}: 8.5in x 14in - @code{Tabloid}: 11in x 17in -
@code{Ledger}: 17in x 11in - @code{A0}: 33.1in x 46.8in - @code{A1}:
23.4in x 33.1in - @code{A2}: 16.5in x 23.4in - @code{A3}: 11.7in x
16.5in - @code{A4}: 8.27in x 11.7in - @code{A5}: 5.83in x 8.27in -
@code{A6}: 4.13in x 5.83in

@quotation
@strong{NOTE} @code{headerTemplate} and @code{footerTemplate} markup
have the following limitations: 1. Script tags inside templates are not
evaluated. 2. Page styles are not visible inside templates.
@end quotation

@node pagequeryObjectsprototypeHandle
@subsection page.queryObjects(prototypeHandle)
@findex page.queryObjects
@anchor{#pagequeryobjectsprototypehandle}
@itemize
@item
@code{prototypeHandle} <@ref{#class-jshandle,JSHandle}> A handle to the
object prototype.
@item
returns:
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise,Promise}<@ref{#class-jshandle,JSHandle}>>
Promise which resolves to a handle to an array of objects with this
prototype.
@end itemize

The method iterates the JavaScript heap and finds all the objects with
the given prototype.

@verbatim
// Create a Map object
await page.evaluate(() => window.map = new Map());
// Get a handle to the Map object prototype
const mapPrototype = await page.evaluateHandle(() => Map.prototype);
// Query all map instances into an array
const mapInstances = await page.queryObjects(mapPrototype);
// Count amount of map objects in heap
const count = await page.evaluate(maps => maps.length, mapInstances);
await mapInstances.dispose();
await mapPrototype.dispose();
@end verbatim

Shortcut for
@ref{#executioncontextqueryobjectsprototypehandle,page.mainFrame().executionContext().queryObjects(prototypeHandle)}.

