@node pagewaitForselectorOrFunctionOrTimeout[ options[@dots{}args]]
@subsection page.waitFor(selectorOrFunctionOrTimeout[, options[,@dots{}args]])
@findex page.waitFor
@anchor{#pagewaitforselectororfunctionortimeout-options-args}
@itemize
@item
@code{selectorOrFunctionOrTimeout}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}|@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type,number}|@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Function,function}>
A
@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_Selectors,selector},
predicate or timeout to wait for
@item
@code{options}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object,Object}>
Optional waiting parameters
@item
@code{...args}
<@dots{}@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/JSON/stringify#Description,Serializable}|@ref{#class-jshandle,JSHandle}>
Arguments to pass to @code{pageFunction}
@item
returns:
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise,Promise}<@ref{#class-jshandle,JSHandle}>>
Promise which resolves to a JSHandle of the success value
@end itemize

This method behaves differently with respect to the type of the first
parameter: - if @code{selectorOrFunctionOrTimeout} is a @code{string},
then the first argument is treated as a
@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_Selectors,selector}
or @uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/XPath,xpath},
depending on whether or not it starts with `//', and the method is a
shortcut for
@ref{#pagewaitforselectorselector-options,page.waitForSelector} or
@ref{#pagewaitforxpathxpath-options,page.waitForXPath} - if
@code{selectorOrFunctionOrTimeout} is a @code{function}, then the first
argument is treated as a predicate to wait for and the method is a
shortcut for
@ref{#pagewaitforfunctionpagefunction-options-args,page.waitForFunction()}.
- if @code{selectorOrFunctionOrTimeout} is a @code{number}, then the
first argument is treated as a timeout in milliseconds and the method
returns a promise which resolves after the timeout - otherwise, an
exception is thrown

@verbatim
// wait for selector
await page.waitFor('.foo');
// wait for 1 second
await page.waitFor(1000);
// wait for predicate
await page.waitFor(() => !!document.querySelector('.foo'));
@end verbatim

To pass arguments from node.js to the predicate of @code{page.waitFor}
function:

@verbatim
const selector = '.foo';
await page.waitFor(selector => !!document.querySelector(selector), {}, selector);
@end verbatim

Shortcut for
@ref{#framewaitforselectororfunctionortimeout-options-args,page.mainFrame().waitFor(selectorOrFunctionOrTimeout[,
options[,@dots{}args]])}.

@node pagewaitForFunctionpageFunction[ options[@dots{}args]]
@subsection page.waitForFunction(pageFunction[, options[,@dots{}args]])
@findex page.waitForFunction
@anchor{#pagewaitforfunctionpagefunction-options-args}
@itemize
@item
@code{pageFunction}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Function,function}|@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}>
Function to be evaluated in browser context
@item
@code{options}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object,Object}>
Optional waiting parameters
@itemize
@item
@code{polling}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#String_type,string}|@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type,number}>
An interval at which the @code{pageFunction} is executed, defaults to
@code{raf}. If @code{polling} is a number, then it is treated as an
interval in milliseconds at which the function would be executed. If
@code{polling} is a string, then it can be one of the following values:
@itemize
@item
@code{raf} - to constantly execute @code{pageFunction} in
@code{requestAnimationFrame} callback. This is the tightest polling mode
which is suitable to observe styling changes.
@item
@code{mutation} - to execute @code{pageFunction} on every DOM mutation.
@end itemize

@item
@code{timeout}
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Number_type,number}>
maximum time to wait for in milliseconds. Defaults to @code{30000} (30
seconds). Pass @code{0} to disable timeout. The default value can be
changed by using the
@ref{#pagesetdefaulttimeouttimeout,page.setDefaultTimeout(timeout)}
method.
@end itemize

@item
@code{...args}
<@dots{}@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/JSON/stringify#Description,Serializable}|@ref{#class-jshandle,JSHandle}>
Arguments to pass to @code{pageFunction}
@item
returns:
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise,Promise}<@ref{#class-jshandle,JSHandle}>>
Promise which resolves when the @code{pageFunction} returns a truthy
value. It resolves to a JSHandle of the truthy value.
@end itemize

The @code{waitForFunction} can be used to observe viewport size change:

@verbatim
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');

puppeteer.launch().then(async browser => {
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  const watchDog = page.waitForFunction('window.innerWidth < 100');
  await page.setViewport({width: 50, height: 50});
  await watchDog;
  await browser.close();
});
@end verbatim

To pass arguments from node.js to the predicate of
@code{page.waitForFunction} function:

@verbatim
const selector = '.foo';
await page.waitForFunction(selector => !!document.querySelector(selector), {}, selector);
@end verbatim

Shortcut for
@ref{#framewaitforfunctionpagefunction-options-args,page.mainFrame().waitForFunction(pageFunction[,
options[,@dots{}args]])}.

