@end itemize

Captures the current state of the accessibility tree. The returned
object represents the root accessible node of the page.

@quotation
@strong{NOTE} The Chromium accessibility tree contains nodes that go
unused on most platforms and by most screen readers. Puppeteer will
discard them as well for an easier to process tree, unless
@code{interestingOnly} is set to @code{false}.
@end quotation
An example of dumping the entire accessibility tree:

@verbatim
const snapshot = await page.accessibility.snapshot();
console.log(snapshot);
@end verbatim

An example of logging the focused node's name:

@verbatim
const snapshot = await page.accessibility.snapshot();
const node = findFocusedNode(snapshot);
console.log(node && node.name);

function findFocusedNode(node) {
  if (node.focused)
    return node;
  for (const child of node.children || []) {
    const foundNode = findFocusedNode(child);
    return foundNode;
  }
  return null;
}
@end verbatim

@node class Keyboard
@section class: Keyboard
@anchor{#class-keyboard}
Keyboard provides an api for managing a virtual keyboard. The high level
api is @ref{#keyboardtypetext-options,@code{keyboard.type}}, which takes
raw characters and generates proper keydown, keypress/input, and keyup
events on your page.

For finer control, you can use
@ref{#keyboarddownkey-options,@code{keyboard.down}},
@ref{#keyboardupkey,@code{keyboard.up}}, and
@ref{#keyboardsendcharacterchar,@code{keyboard.sendCharacter}} to
manually fire events as if they were generated from a real keyboard.

An example of holding down @code{Shift} in order to select and delete
some text:

@verbatim
await page.keyboard.type('Hello World!');
await page.keyboard.press('ArrowLeft');

await page.keyboard.down('Shift');
for (let i = 0; i < ' World'.length; i++)
  await page.keyboard.press('ArrowLeft');
await page.keyboard.up('Shift');

await page.keyboard.press('Backspace');
// Result text will end up saying 'Hello!'
@end verbatim

An example of pressing @code{A}

@verbatim
await page.keyboard.down('Shift');
await page.keyboard.press('KeyA');
await page.keyboard.up('Shift');
@end verbatim

@quotation
@strong{NOTE} On MacOS, keyboard shortcuts like @code{⌘ A} -> Select All
do not work. See
@uref{https://github.com/GoogleChrome/puppeteer/issues/1313,#1313}
@end quotation

