@end itemize

@item
returns:
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise,Promise}>
Promise which resolves when the element matching @code{selector} is
successfully clicked. The Promise will be rejected if there is no
element matching @code{selector}.
@end itemize

This method fetches an element with @code{selector}, scrolls it into
view if needed, and then uses @ref{#pagemouse,page.mouse} to click in
the center of the element. If there's no element matching
@code{selector}, the method throws an error.

Bear in mind that if @code{click()} triggers a navigation event and
there's a separate @code{page.waitForNavigation()} promise to be
resolved, you may end up with a race condition that yields unexpected
results. The correct pattern for click and wait for navigation is the
following:

@verbatim
const [response] = await Promise.all([
  page.waitForNavigation(waitOptions),
  frame.click(selector, clickOptions),
]);
@end verbatim

