@node class ElementHandle
@section class: ElementHandle
@anchor{#class-elementhandle}
@itemize
@item
extends: @ref{#class-jshandle,JSHandle}
@end itemize

ElementHandle represents an in-page DOM element. ElementHandles can be
created with the @ref{#pageselector,page.$} method.

@verbatim
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');

puppeteer.launch().then(async browser => {
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.goto('https://example.com');
  const hrefElement = await page.$('a');
  await hrefElement.click();
  // ...
});
@end verbatim

ElementHandle prevents DOM element from garbage collection unless the
handle is @ref{#elementhandledispose,disposed}. ElementHandles are
auto-disposed when their origin frame gets navigated.

ElementHandle instances can be used as arguments in
@ref{#pageevalselector-pagefunction-args,@code{page.$eval()}} and
@ref{#pageevaluatepagefunction-args,@code{page.evaluate()}} methods.

