@node class Request
@section class: Request
@anchor{#class-request}
Whenever the page sends a request, such as for a network resource, the
following events are emitted by puppeteer's page: -
@ref{#event-request,`request'} emitted when the request is issued by the
page. - @ref{#event-response,`response'} emitted when/if the response is
received for the request. -
@ref{#event-requestfinished,`requestfinished'} emitted when the response
body is downloaded and the request is complete.

If request fails at some point, then instead of `requestfinished' event
(and possibly instead of `response' event), the
@ref{#event-requestfailed,`requestfailed'} event is emitted.

If request gets a `redirect' response, the request is successfully
finished with the `requestfinished' event, and a new request is issued
to a redirected url.

