@node requestredirectChain
@subsection request.redirectChain()
@findex request.redirectChain
@anchor{#requestredirectchain}
@itemize
@item
returns:
<@uref{https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array,Array}<@ref{#class-request,Request}>>
@end itemize

A @code{redirectChain} is a chain of requests initiated to fetch a
resource. - If there are no redirects and the request was successful,
the chain will be empty. - If a server responds with at least a single
redirect, then the chain will contain all the requests that were
redirected.

@code{redirectChain} is shared between all the requests of the same
chain.

For example, if the website @code{http://example.com} has a single
redirect to @code{https://example.com}, then the chain will contain one
request:

@verbatim
const response = await page.goto('http://example.com');
const chain = response.request().redirectChain();
console.log(chain.length); // 1
console.log(chain[0].url()); // 'http://example.com'
@end verbatim

If the website @code{https://google.com} has no redirects, then the
chain will be empty:

@verbatim
const response = await page.goto('https://google.com');
const chain = response.request().redirectChain();
console.log(chain.length); // 0
@end verbatim

