@section class: CDPSession
@anchor{#class-cdpsession}
@itemize
@item
extends:
@uref{https://nodejs.org/api/events.html#events_class_eventemitter,EventEmitter}
@end itemize

The @code{CDPSession} instances are used to talk raw Chrome Devtools
Protocol: - protocol methods can be called with @code{session.send}
method. - protocol events can be subscribed to with @code{session.on}
method.

Useful links: - Documentation on DevTools Protocol can be found here:
@uref{https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/,DevTools
Protocol Viewer}. - Getting Started with DevTools Protocol:
https://github.com/aslushnikov/getting-started-with-cdp/blob/master/README.md

@verbatim
const client = await page.target().createCDPSession();
await client.send('Animation.enable');
client.on('Animation.animationCreated', () => console.log('Animation created!'));
const response = await client.send('Animation.getPlaybackRate');
console.log('playback rate is ' + response.playbackRate);
await client.send('Animation.setPlaybackRate', {
  playbackRate: response.playbackRate / 2
});
@end verbatim

