Coverage gathers information about parts of JavaScript and CSS that were
used by the page.

An example of using JavaScript and CSS coverage to get percentage of
initially executed code:

@verbatim
// Enable both JavaScript and CSS coverage
await Promise.all([
  page.coverage.startJSCoverage(),
  page.coverage.startCSSCoverage()
]);
// Navigate to page
await page.goto('https://example.com');
// Disable both JavaScript and CSS coverage
const [jsCoverage, cssCoverage] = await Promise.all([
  page.coverage.stopJSCoverage(),
  page.coverage.stopCSSCoverage(),
]);
let totalBytes = 0;
let usedBytes = 0;
const coverage = [...jsCoverage, ...cssCoverage];
for (const entry of coverage) {
  totalBytes += entry.text.length;
  for (const range of entry.ranges)
    usedBytes += range.end - range.start - 1;
}
console.log(`Bytes used: ${usedBytes / totalBytes * 100}%`);
@end verbatim

@emph{To output coverage in a form consumable by
@uref{https://github.com/istanbuljs,Istanbul}, see
@uref{https://github.com/istanbuljs/puppeteer-to-istanbul,puppeteer-to-istanbul}.}

